                <pb facs="0145" n="133" sameAs="frus:frus1942v05/pg133"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">810.74/378: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Chile</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Bowers</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Santiago</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1942-07-23T21:00:00-05:00">July 23, 1942—9
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 10 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1202. For Under Secretary. Your telegram No. 827, July 22, 7 p.m. I understand
                    the point absolutely and I have made entirely clear to the Minister.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Bowers</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
